                <pb facs="0482" n="466" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg466"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.6363/12–2447: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Key</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-12-24T08:00:00-03:00">December 24,
                            1947—8 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1740. Under pressure from President Dutra urgent solution Brazil’s petroleum
                    problem General Barreto, President National Petroleum Council, has approached
                    Embassy requesting following information: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Can U. S. Government charter or sell to Brazil up to four fuel oil
                            tankers; if so how many, carrying capacity, what price.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Can U. S. guarantee or assure Brazil’s minimum requirements petroleum
                            products first 6 months 1948, amounts as submitted by Brazilian Embassy
                            Washington to Office International Trade July 1947 in reply to latter’s
                            request for such information.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Would appreciate Department’s comment soonest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Key</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
